      "content": "hey i need help with something weird. i was doing an internship at the lab last month and there was a leak in the particle stream chamber while i was calibrating. nothing felt wrong at the time but lately i've been seeing these... i don't know how to describe it... colored mists in my peripheral vision? like, right before something happens. like if a car is gonna swerve i'll see this thick red cloud. it's not like a hallucination because it's too consistent. is there any way the radiation could have actually changed how i perceive probability or something??",
